how to win at arm wrestling and roll to  victory with expert advice from Neal  pickup as someone just challenged you to  an arm wrestle well lucky for you or  perhaps for your opponent arm wrestling  isn't just about brute strength using  the right technique will not only help  me to win but will also help you avoid  any injuries the most effective arm  wrestling technique and the best way to  quickly win is the top role in a third  century BC the Greek mathematician  Archimedes famously stated give me a  lever long enough and a fulcrum on which  to place it and I shall move the world  what's that got to do with armwrestling  I hear you ask well actually everything  your forearm is the lever and you want  to make it as long as possible and your  elbow is the fulcrum or pivot points  which you need to be strong so stand as  close to the table as you can and took  your elbow into your body allowing the  muscles in your back shoulder and arm to  provide support when you grip your  opponent's hand face your knuckles  directly to the ceiling creating the  highest possible position for your hand  to be in as soon as the contest starts  lean your body back and pull your hands  straight towards your nose this  technique will break open your  challengers hand as soon as their grip  begins to slip pull your arm diagonally  towards your other shoulder dropping  your knees and dipping your waist at the  same time you've just neutralized your  rivals forum until you rolling your body  down until you inevitably taste victory  the brilliance of the top rope apart  from the sense of superiority you now  feel is that you have not had to use any  joints but made most effective use of  your muscle power so even if your  adversary fights back you will not hurt  your arm  but don't  get overconfident the top roll is good  [Music]
 

